      "message": "You\u0027re right that only one new binding appears here — that\u0027s expected.\n \nOAuthServiceProvider is already an bound extension point, unchanged by this commit. \n\nThe change adds two default methods to it — supportsRevoke() / revoke(OAuthToken) — so a provider gets the revoke capability with no new binding.\n\nThe only new extension point is OAuthTokenRevokedListener, which is why it\u0027s the single new DynamicSet.setOf(...) line. Example implementation in the `oauth` plugin: change 634160 (OAuthTokenValidationCacheCleaner).\n\nI\u0027ve adapted the commit message.",
